    "notes": "The Pacific Northwest's quiet station: indie folk (playtest 2, 2026-10-02: \"There should be different stations and music in different regions\"). Since playtest 4 (P4-17: \"indie and folk with drive\") each track is a whole sixteen-bar song in a major key at 116-148 bpm: a strummed intro, a verse with the glockenspiel tune, a build, then a driving chorus (four-on-the-floor stomp, sixteenth tambourine, banjo rolls, the hook and a tremolo mandolin) (src/audio/radio-compose-pnw.ts, preset folk-band). Melodies are generated from each track's seed, so they are original. No DJ lines yet (djBarkSet null). Cut a track by setting its status to vetoed.",
